63,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Now that we know the candidates, I'm leaning toward the Wetland Restoration. It fits the habitat fund and seems like it wouldn't need as much heavy digging in the center as a plaza would.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I disagree, Kenji. The Wetland Restoration would likely disrupt the firm, open ground that commuters use for the tram stop, and the drainage issues we've seen suggest a risk of failure.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think the Woodland Walk could be nice, but the Sports Terraces might be better because we already have volunteers who like refereeing youth league games.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Minako,,The Woodland Walk is too risky given the eastern avenue's failure; we cannot trust a plan that relies so heavily on tree survival without a guaranteed maintenance contract.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I find the Market Plaza financially attractive for long-term upkeep, but the loss of the habitat fund makes it a capital nightmare. The Wetland Restoration is the only one that solves our funding gap.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, but if we do the Wetland Restoration, we can use the habitat fund to pay for it! Plus, the earth-moving firms said shallow work is fine, and ponds are better than huge slabs of concrete.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, shallow work is one thing, but the drainage callouts indicate the ground is already struggling. Adding ponds could exacerbate the issue if not engineered perfectly, and it still blocks the tram commuters.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, but the Wetland Restoration might actually help the drainage problems you mentioned! And the habitat volunteers are already working upriver, so they would probably love to help here.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, that is a valid point. If the overflow basin from the previous programme is still functioning well, it proves that water-management schemes are the most durable option we have.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I am beginning to agree. If the overflow basin is a success and we have the habitat fund for capital, the Wetland Restoration is the most fiscally responsible choice despite the higher upkeep.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm glad we're agreeing! The Wetland Restoration seems like the best fit for the funding, the volunteers, and the soil risks. I'm definitely voting for that one!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I still have reservations about the commuter paths, but the evidence of the overflow basin's durability is a compelling counter-argument to my concerns about the ground's stability.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'll vote for the Wetland Restoration too! It uses the habitat fund, helps the drainage, and the volunteers can help look after it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I agree. Given the success of the previous water-management works and the existing volunteer support, the Wetland Restoration is the most sustainable and reliable choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I will also vote for the Wetland Restoration. It is the only plan that aligns with our capital funding while remaining manageable through the support of the existing volunteer groups.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all agree! I'll cast my vote for the Wetland Restoration. It's the best way to make the park great without breaking the bank or the ground!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While I remain cautious about the pedestrian flow, the logic of the funding and the durability of the basin prevail. I cast my vote for the Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm really glad we could find a solution that helps the environment and the people. I vote for the Wetland Restoration!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Minako,,I believe this is the most rational decision based on the evidence. I cast my vote for the Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I concur. For the sake of financial stability and long-term viability, I cast my vote for the Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
